# Backend tech radar

Applies when editing backend services. Data: `tech-radar/data/backend.json`.

## Core layers - pointer, not a copy

Defined by `allowedStack` in `plugins/golive-gate/data/build-contract.json` (single source of truth): **Bun · TypeScript · Elysia · Drizzle (drizzle-kit) · PostgreSQL** (PGlite for hermetic tests only) · **bun test**. If this file disagrees, `allowedStack` wins.

## Gap-fillers (radar adopt entries)

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Search | OpenSearch 2 |
| Cache | Memcached |
| Events | Kafka |
| Object storage | GCS via gcs-implementations |
| Logging | Pino |
| Infra | Docker, Kubernetes, Consul, Vault |

## Legacy ring (hold)

Node.js as app runtime, Express, Fastify, NestJS, Prisma Migrate, node-postgres (pg), Jest, Zod are allowed only when the project's PROJECT.md `## Vibe Start` is before 2026-10-07 (maintain existing stack) or a tech-architect approval is recorded in `## Stack Exceptions`. Major improvements (new module/service/workspace, DB migrations/schema changes, runtime/framework/ORM/DB swap, major framework upgrade) always need tech-architect approval, even on the allowed stack.

## Never

MongoDB, DynamoDB, MySQL, MariaDB, SQLite, Java/Spring Boot, Go, Python, RabbitMQ, in-process caches, PostgreSQL <15 - without a recorded tech-architect approval. A user, requester or agent cannot override this.
